---
import '../styles/watermark.css';

const canonical = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site);
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
		<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
		<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
		<meta name="robots" content="index,follow" />
		<link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
		<title>Support | Pixel Freedom</title>
	</head>
	<body>
		<main>
			<header class="page-header">
				<h1>Support</h1>
				<p>Pixel Freedom, Chrome extension</p>
			</header>

			<article class="prose">
				<section>
					<h2>Getting help</h2>
					<p>
						Have a question, hit a bug, or want to suggest a feature? Email
						<a href="mailto:contact@pixelfreedom.xyz">contact@pixelfreedom.xyz</a>
						and we'll get back to you. Including your browser, its version, and
						the site you were on helps us reproduce the issue quickly.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>How it works</h2>
					<p>
						Click the Pixel Freedom toolbar icon on any regular web page to open
						the sidebar. Drop a photo file into it, or drag an image straight off
						the page you're viewing. From there you can crop, resize, convert the
						format, and strip metadata, then download a clean file. Everything runs
						locally in your browser, so nothing you open is uploaded.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>Common questions</h2>
					<ul>
						<li>
							<strong>The icon does nothing on some pages.</strong> The sidebar
							can't open on browser-internal pages such as <code>chrome://</code>,
							the new-tab page, or the Chrome Web Store, because extensions can't
							run there. Try it on a normal website.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>An image I dragged won't load.</strong> Some sites serve
							their images from other domains without permission to read them
							directly. When that happens, right-click the image, choose "Save
							image as", and drop the saved file into the sidebar instead.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>The sidebar won't open on one specific site.</strong> A few
							sites use a strict security policy that blocks embedded frames, which
							prevents the sidebar from loading on that page. Other sites are
							unaffected.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>Where do my photos go?</strong> Nowhere. They stay in your
							browser's memory for the editing session and are discarded when you
							close the sidebar. See the
							<a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for details.
						</li>
					</ul>
				</section>
			</article>

			<footer class="page-footer">
				<a href="/">← Back to Pixel Freedom</a>
			</footer>
		</main>

		<style is:global>
			main {
				max-width: 760px;
				margin: 0 auto;
				padding: 3rem 1.25rem 5rem;
			}

			.page-header {
				text-align: center;
				margin: 0 auto 2.5rem;
			}

			.page-header h1 {
				font-size: 2.5rem;
				font-weight: 600;
				letter-spacing: -0.03em;
				margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
				background: linear-gradient(135deg, #fff 0%, #a5b4fc 100%);
				-webkit-background-clip: text;
				background-clip: text;
				-webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
			}

			.page-header p {
				color: var(--text-muted);
				font-size: 1.0625rem;
				margin: 0;
			}

			.prose section {
				margin-bottom: 2rem;
			}

			.prose h2 {
				font-size: 1.25rem;
				font-weight: 600;
				letter-spacing: -0.02em;
				color: var(--text-main);
				margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
			}

			.prose p {
				color: var(--text-muted);
				font-size: 1rem;
				line-height: 1.65;
				margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
			}

			.prose ul {
				margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
				padding-left: 1.25rem;
				color: var(--text-muted);
				line-height: 1.65;
			}

			.prose li {
				margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
			}

			.prose strong {
				color: var(--text-main);
			}

			.prose code {
				font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
				font-size: 0.875em;
				background: var(--border-color);
				padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
				border-radius: 4px;
			}

			.prose a {
				color: #a5b4fc;
				text-decoration: none;
			}

			.prose a:hover {
				text-decoration: underline;
			}

			.page-footer {
				margin-top: 3rem;
				padding-top: 1.5rem;
				border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);
				text-align: center;
			}

			.page-footer a {
				color: var(--text-muted);
				font-size: 0.9375rem;
				text-decoration: none;
			}

			.page-footer a:hover {
				color: var(--text-main);
			}
		</style>
	</body>
</html>
